{
  "dom_id": "step-q131532",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\u03a6(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ compute $P(Z<-0.73).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7673\\,$ | $\\,0.7704\\,$ | $\\,0.7734\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7967\\,$ | $\\,0.7995\\,$ | $\\,0.8023\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.8238\\,$ | $\\,0.8264\\,$ | $\\,0.8289\\,$ |",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/597125714057269b7adf9c0a2a9bbdde9631cf37bc80518281ab4444c3189717.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ we have the following symmetry property for $a>0:$\n\n$$\nP(Z>a)=P(Z<-a)=\u03a6(-a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z<-0.73).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/3e4fb2143266d45a620bf39a978ba8ac4f0ed2585942f79dc90435a4896f9a0d.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z>0.73).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/6bb24449a20276b9d190e2b31926bb6e0d52f22536431e27c05db00b92886ffc.png)\n\nNote that the two shaded areas above have the same area. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z<-0.73) & =P(Z>0.73) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<0.73) \\\\  & =1-\u03a6(0.73) \\\\  & =1-0.7673 \\\\  & =0.2327.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
